comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-02T13:30:35.914Z","harness:claude-code","Context from pm-gh1576 (expected item revisions, same PR family): the global --expect-hash precondition is now available on pm test. The advertised two-step retry could carry --expect-hash <item_hash> on its removal step, so a list changed between the refusal and the retry refuses with item_revision_conflict instead of removing a different entry. That only narrows the race: the add step still runs as a separate mutation, so this item's atomic single-mutation replacement (one locked write, identity-collision refusal) remains the open acceptance. The refusal would also need to report the current item_hash for the retry to cite it."
body: ""
